#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:4
msgid "Hexagon boot interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:6
msgid ""
"``qemu-system-hexagon`` loads the initial image. Guest startup code "
"initializes the stack, exception handling, and runtime state. When a Hexagon "
"VM host is loaded, it establishes the guest OS's boot environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:11
msgid "Initial hardware state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:13
msgid ""
"Only hardware thread zero starts executing. Other threads start powered off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:16
msgid ""
"Execution uses untranslated physical addresses in monitor mode. Guest "
"software must populate TLB entries before enabling the MMU, and set up "
"exception vectors and interrupt masks before enabling interrupts. "
"See :doc:`../../devel/hexagon-sys` for the system architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:21
msgid ""
"QEMU sets thread zero's PC to the selected image entry address. ``EVB`` "
"initially contains zero; ELF startup code installs its own aligned event "
"vector base."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:26
msgid "Simulator-compatible machines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:28
msgid ""
"``-kernel file`` loads a little-endian Hexagon ELF, places its loadable "
"segments according to their physical addresses, zero-fills the segments' "
"remaining memory, and starts thread zero at the ELF entry point. Link "
"startup code for untranslated execution, with the entry point accessible at "
"its linked address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:35
msgid "The virt machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:37
msgid ""
"``-kernel file`` alone loads a Hexagon ELF into DDR, which starts at "
"``0x80000000``, and starts at its ELF entry point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:40
msgid ""
"``-bios file`` alone loads a raw firmware image at the start of DDR and "
"starts executing there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:43
msgid ""
"``-bios`` with ``-kernel`` boots the kernel through Hexagon VM host "
"firmware, as described in :ref:`hexagon-vm-boot`. Both ELF images load at "
"their declared physical addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:47
msgid ""
"Otherwise, guest software reads the generated DTB at ``0x99800000``. ``-"
"append`` sets its ``/chosen/bootargs`` property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:51
msgid "Board-specific machines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:53
msgid ""
"Both ``-kernel`` and ``-bios`` accept Hexagon ELF images. The combinations "
"have different meanings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:59
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:60
msgid "Loading and entry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:61
msgid "``-kernel`` alone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:62
msgid "Load segments at ELF physical addresses and start at the ELF entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:63
msgid "``-bios`` alone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:64
msgid ""
"Load firmware segments at ELF physical addresses and start at its entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:65
msgid "``-bios`` and ``-kernel``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:66
msgid ""
"Load firmware normally, relocate the kernel segments into the board's kernel "
"window, and enter firmware through a QEMU boot stub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:69
msgid ""
"The combined case is described in :ref:`hexagon-vm-boot`, using the kernel "
"base in :doc:`cdsp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:72
msgid ""
"``-dtb file`` replaces the generated tree. A nonempty ``-append`` value sets "
"its ``/chosen/bootargs``. A replacement tree must describe the selected "
"hardware-thread count, actual RAM, and matching device drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:79
msgid "Booting a kernel through Hexagon VM host firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:81
msgid ""
"On the ``virt`` and board-specific machines, ``-bios`` with ``-kernel`` "
"starts the kernel through Hexagon VM host firmware. QEMU loads the firmware "
"ELF as linked. On ``virt``, it also loads the kernel ELF as linked. The "
"board-specific machines add their configured kernel base to the kernel ELF's "
"physical load addresses, so those kernels are relative to the start of the "
"board's guest window. QEMU starts thread zero at a boot stub at "
"``0x99c00000``. The stub passes the DTB address with the low word in ``r0`` "
"and the high word in ``r1``, then jumps to the firmware's ELF entry point. "
"The Hexagon VM host defines the child VM's register and execution state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:91
msgid ""
"QEMU places the DTB after the loaded kernel.  QEMU copies it to guest RAM "
"before entering the firmware. An optional ``-initrd`` is placed after the "
"DTB base.  ``-initrd`` requires both ``-bios`` and ``-kernel``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:96
msgid "Console and semihosting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/boot.rst:98
msgid ""
"SDK simulator programs use semihosting for console I/O. The ``virt`` and "
"board-specific machines also provide a PL011 UART, whose host backend is "
"selected with ``-serial``."
msgstr ""
